          "turn_index": 1,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Is that enough to need something preventive?",
          "answer": "Preventive measures for migraines are typically recommended if a person experiences frequent attacks. While the exact threshold can vary, many clinicians consider preventive treatment if a person has migraines on 4 or more days per month, or if the attacks are particularly severe or disabling (source: National headache society guidance).\n\nSince you mentioned experiencing migraines six times a month, it would be reasonable to discuss the option of preventive measures with a clinician. They can help assess the frequency, severity, and impact of your migraines and determine if preventive treatment might be beneficial for you.\n\nBe sure to address any concerns about your migraine patterns during your discussion so that you can explore suitable preventive options.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
